{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.OrientedSkein.SkeinDatum","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.SkeinDatum","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Rigid.Braided","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidedSlide","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidedQuantumDimension","lean:module:QOU.OrientedSkein.HeckeCrossing"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.OrientedSkeinDatum.ofBraided_T","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.OrientedSkeinDatum.ofBraided_T","kind":"theorem","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/SkeinDatum.lean#L188-L191","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.OrientedSkeinDatum.ofBraided_S","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.OrientedSkeinDatum.ofBraided_S","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/SkeinDatum.lean#L183-L186","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.OrientedSkeinDatum.ofBraided","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.OrientedSkeinDatum.ofBraided","kind":"def","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/SkeinDatum.lean#L163-L181","doc":"**A Hecke braiding gives oriented skein data.**  In an `R`-linear braided monoidal category, if\n`F ⊣ E` is an exact pairing, the self-braiding `β_{E,E}` satisfies the Hecke relation\n`β² = (q - qi) β + (q qi) 1`, and the braided quantum dimension `qDimWith F E = η ≫ β_{F,E} ≫ ε`\nsatisfies `t · qDimWith F E = δ · 1`, then `S = β_{E,E}`, `T = β_{F,E}`, `C = η`, `D = ε` is\noriented skein data.  Relations (2) and (4) hold in every braided category\n(`braid_braiding`, `sideways_braiding`); (1) and (5) are exactly the two hypotheses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.sideways_braiding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.sideways_braiding","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/SkeinDatum.lean#L136-L151","doc":"**Relation (4) for a braiding.**  The sideways rotation of the self-braiding `β_{E,E}` is the\ninverse of the mixed braiding `β_{F,E}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.cup_cross","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.cup_cross","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/SkeinDatum.lean#L121-L134","doc":"Sliding the cup past the self-braiding: the strand `E` crossing the newly created `E` leg of\nthe cup `η : 𝟙 ⟶ F ⊗ E` is the same as `E` crossing the `F` leg with the inverse braiding. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.braid_braiding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.braid_braiding","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/SkeinDatum.lean#L115-L119","doc":"The self-braiding satisfies the braid relation (2): this is the Yang–Baxter equation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.OrientedSkeinDatum.heckeAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.OrientedSkeinDatum.heckeAction","kind":"def","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/SkeinDatum.lean#L101-L105","doc":"Brundan's `ι_r : H_r → End(E^{⊗ r})`, for oriented skein data in any `R`-linear monoidal\ncategory. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.OrientedSkeinDatum.dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.OrientedSkeinDatum.dim","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/SkeinDatum.lean#L95-L95","doc":"Relation (5): `t · D ∘ T ∘ C = δ · 1_𝟙`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.OrientedSkeinDatum.sideways_T","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.OrientedSkeinDatum.sideways_T","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/SkeinDatum.lean#L93-L93","doc":"Relation (4), second half. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.OrientedSkeinDatum.T_sideways","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.OrientedSkeinDatum.T_sideways","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/SkeinDatum.lean#L91-L91","doc":"Relation (4), first half. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.OrientedSkeinDatum.T","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.OrientedSkeinDatum.T","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/SkeinDatum.lean#L89-L89","doc":"The mixed crossing `T`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.OrientedSkeinDatum.cross","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.OrientedSkeinDatum.cross","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/SkeinDatum.lean#L87-L87","doc":"The crossing `S` with relations (1) and (2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.OrientedSkeinDatum.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.OrientedSkeinDatum.mk","kind":"ctor","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/SkeinDatum.lean#L85-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.OrientedSkeinDatum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.OrientedSkeinDatum","kind":"structure","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/SkeinDatum.lean#L82-L95","doc":"**Oriented skein data** in an `R`-linear monoidal category: the images of Brundan's\ngenerators `E, F, S, T, C = η, D = ε` satisfying his relations (1)–(5).  Here `qi` is the intended\ninverse of `q` (so `z = q - qi`) and `δ` the intended value of `(t - t⁻¹)/z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.sideways","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.sideways","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/SkeinDatum.lean#L76-L80","doc":"Brundan's **sideways crossing**: the rotation of `S : E ⊗ E ⟶ E ⊗ E` by the cup\n`η : 𝟙 ⟶ F ⊗ E` and the cap `ε : E ⊗ F ⟶ 𝟙`,\n`(1_F ⊗ 1_E ⊗ D) ∘ (1_F ⊗ S ⊗ 1_F) ∘ (C ⊗ 1_E ⊗ 1_F) : E ⊗ F ⟶ F ⊗ E`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}